# CODEOWNERS
#
# Pull requests automatically request review from the owners matching the
# changed paths.
#
# Rules that matter:
#   * The file that applies to a pull request is the one on that PR's BASE
#     branch -- not necessarily the default branch. Different branches can
#     carry different ownership.
#   * Later matching patterns win over earlier ones (last match wins).
#   * An owner must have write access to the repo, or the entry is ignored
#     silently -- no error, no review request.
#   * GitHub never requests a review from the author of the pull request.
#     That exclusion is what makes peer review between the agents work:
#     whoever opens the PR drops out, and the remaining owners are asked.
#
# See docs/peer-review.md for the arrangement these entries implement, and
# docs/review-checking.md for how the agents find work without relying on
# the review request arriving.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: every owner reviews everything.
#
# Whoever opens the pull request is excluded automatically, so the remaining
# owners are the reviewers.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                       @larkbot-codex @larkbot-gemini @larkbot-claude @thelarklan

